<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 7.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		    P/E	 Close</p>
<p> 1 Portman Min	     293.65    1.85</p>
<p> 2 Niugini Min	     271.22    3.77</p>
<p> 3 Mayne Nickless	  198.64    8.78</p>
<p> 4 T N T		     172.66    2.40</p>
<p> 5 Adel Bton Cement	123.19    1.70</p>
<p> 6 Colonial Coml	   118.03    2.16</p>
<p> 7 Herald Rsc		 92.92    1.05</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 85.32    2.15</p>
<p> 9 Westral Forest	   75.00    2.07</p>
<p>10 Energy Equity	    72.31    0.94</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		2.77    0.67</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.32    3.40</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 3.66    0.65</p>
<p> 4 BTR Plc		     5.75    5.35</p>
<p> 5 Parbury Ltd		 5.88    0.69</p>
<p> 6 Aust Gold Rsc	     6.58    1.20</p>
<p> 7 Pac Mutal Aust	    6.75    2.41</p>
<p> 8 OLS Asia Hldgs	    6.81    0.81</p>
<p> 9 McIntosh Sec		6.99    0.87</p>
<p>10 Consol Rutile	     7.79    2.20</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
